WEBVTT

00:00:17.530 --> 00:00:22.080
I'm sorry for shoving senpais aside
and volunteering to come with you.

00:00:22.330 --> 00:00:26.080
Don't worry. Flat and Svin
are on extracurricular lessons anyway.

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:28.460
Make sure to be very careful
while you're on the train.

00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:30.300
Is it a dangerous train?

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:33.470
Rail Zeppelin.

00:00:34.090 --> 00:00:36.430
It's a train that superhuman
vampires created

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:38.850
to make deals with Mystic Eyes.

00:00:39.810 --> 00:00:41.970
Its existence itself is equal
to that of the underworld.

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:51.280
It's possible that one of those customers
is the culprit who stole the Relic.

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:52.940
Even if they aren't,

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:56.240
only supernatural beings
would board this train.

00:00:57.030 --> 00:00:59.830
So that's why you brought glasses
that eradicate Mystic Eyes.

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:01.660
You really make good preparations.

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:03.370
Hishiri Adashino!

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:04.830
You again?

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:11.130
I expected you to be on the move
based on the materials concerning Wills.

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:14.130
I was thinking some Lord was here,

00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:16.510
but I didn't expect the rumored
Modern Magecraft Theories.

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:18.930
It has been a while, Lady.

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:24.310
Even the figurehead of Norwich
recognizes my face at the least?

00:01:24.770 --> 00:01:25.980
It's Olga-Marie.

00:01:26.230 --> 00:01:28.810
Olga-Marie Arsimilat Animusphere.

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:32.820
She's the daughter
of the Lord of Astromancy.

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:36.740
So, do you have some particular
Mystic Eyes you're after?

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:39.030
We'll see about that, won't we?

00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:40.570
I'll make this clear,

00:01:40.830 --> 00:01:43.830
but Astromancy will make sure
to win this year's auction.

00:01:44.290 --> 00:01:46.960
Even if I'm up against a Lord,
I'm not going to go easy.

00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:49.580
It seems you overestimate me.

00:01:49.580 --> 00:01:51.590
My lady, it's almost time.

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:53.840
All right, Trisha.

00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:57.420
In any case, I ask you one thing.
Don't get in the way of Animusphere!

00:01:57.720 --> 00:01:59.090
So scary, so scary.

00:01:59.470 --> 00:02:00.680
My lady.

00:02:05.390 --> 00:02:09.060
It's unusual for an Animusphere
to descend from the mountains.

00:02:09.350 --> 00:02:13.980
It's natural for Astromancy to show interest
in Mystic Eyes that can predict the Mystics.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:27.000
Let's go.

00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:02.090
Somehow,

00:04:02.470 --> 00:04:04.680
this place is larger than it looks.

00:04:05.550 --> 00:04:06.470
I told you, didn't I?

00:04:06.890 --> 00:04:08.600
This train itself...

00:04:08.890 --> 00:04:09.970
is the underworld.

00:04:11.350 --> 00:04:14.140
But they sure are all notable figures.

00:04:28.280 --> 00:04:30.240
<i>I know the faces of half of them,</i>

00:04:30.830 --> 00:04:32.500
<i>but they're all monsters.</i>

00:04:35.620 --> 00:04:36.540
<i>No way!</i>

00:04:43.420 --> 00:04:45.090
Karabo Frampton...

00:04:45.510 --> 00:04:47.180
from the Holy Church.

00:04:53.730 --> 00:04:56.440
Impossible!
The Holy Church came out here?

00:04:56.770 --> 00:04:59.770
The one that contends
against the Clock Tower?

00:05:02.570 --> 00:05:05.780
Stop it. I don't mean
to stir up any trouble here.

00:05:06.030 --> 00:05:07.990
I'm going to participate
in the auction, as well.

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:09.160
Do you object?

00:05:09.490 --> 00:05:10.740
Pardon me.

00:05:11.080 --> 00:05:13.700
No, that reaction was to be expected.

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:18.080
No way! Sir El-Melloi II is here, too?

00:05:18.290 --> 00:05:19.840
Welcome aboard!

00:05:20.090 --> 00:05:20.920
It's you...

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:22.960
Yvette! Why are you here?

00:05:24.170 --> 00:05:26.510
My family is an authority of Mystic Eyes!

00:05:26.930 --> 00:05:31.260
We're regulars of the auction on
the Mystic Eyes Collection Train! It's for sure!

00:05:37.100 --> 00:05:40.110
Oh, but I didn't expect
Caules to be here, too.

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:42.480
Are you one of his sycophants?

00:05:42.480 --> 00:05:45.900
No, though it's true
that I asked him to be here.

00:05:48.110 --> 00:05:50.620
Sir, it's not good to be cheating!

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:56.580
Oh no, maybe BL can be a thing?
I'm sorry if I'm not good with multiplay!

00:05:56.830 --> 00:05:57.870
How cute.

00:05:58.120 --> 00:05:59.210
You want to be his mistress?

00:05:59.420 --> 00:06:01.460
Yes! I'm a regular
at sneaking into the bedroom!

00:06:01.880 --> 00:06:03.340
All right, you stay quiet.

00:06:03.590 --> 00:06:06.340
If possible, jump out of that window
right this second.

00:06:06.590 --> 00:06:09.800
Pardon the interruption
of your pleasant chat.

00:06:10.090 --> 00:06:14.810
I'm Leandra, and I'll be
the auctioneer for this train.

00:06:15.060 --> 00:06:16.730
And I'm Rodin, the conductor.

00:06:17.600 --> 00:06:22.060
And now, Rail Zeppelin
will be departing as scheduled.

00:06:27.070 --> 00:06:28.950
The auction in three days' time

00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:32.490
will have many prized Mystic Eyes
from our collection.

00:06:33.160 --> 00:06:36.290
Please make sure to spend
your time here with no regrets.

00:06:39.250 --> 00:06:40.540
But...

00:06:40.790 --> 00:06:43.630
the one who invited me never showed up.

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:45.380
Shall we go look for him?

00:06:45.750 --> 00:06:49.680
Stop it. Something will surely happen
now that I've been lured out.

00:06:49.930 --> 00:06:53.140
There's no good in simply worrying
under our current conditions.

00:06:55.180 --> 00:06:56.140
Sir?

00:06:56.390 --> 00:06:57.560
Let me sleep.

00:06:57.810 --> 00:06:59.890
I was up all night last night, too.

00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:20.160
This must be it.

00:07:24.250 --> 00:07:26.670
Welcome, Kairi Shishigou.

00:07:29.090 --> 00:07:32.590
I didn't think I'd be called over
to a fancy place like this.

00:07:33.010 --> 00:07:36.100
Though, I can't imagine that it would
suit your palette, Lady Reines.

00:07:36.470 --> 00:07:38.810
This is a place
my elder brother patronizes.

00:07:39.270 --> 00:07:41.850
Besides, they serve delicious sandwiches.

00:07:43.020 --> 00:07:43.900
So,

00:07:44.230 --> 00:07:48.360
what does the little sister of a Lord want
with a freelance Magician like me?

00:07:48.860 --> 00:07:52.360
My brother's catalyst
for the Holy Grail War has been stolen.

00:07:53.240 --> 00:07:56.160
You can't mean the ritual utensil
to summon a Heroic Spirit!

00:07:56.530 --> 00:08:00.660
What was stolen is the mantle
of Iskandar, King of Conquerors.

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:03.830
That's quite an item to bring out.

00:08:03.830 --> 00:08:07.550
Yes. It was something
that Kayneth specially obtained.

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:09.420
The mantle of the King of Conquerors...

00:08:09.670 --> 00:08:14.680
could create a magical bond with Iskandar
or one of his subordinates.

00:08:17.010 --> 00:08:20.720
That's something any Necromancer
would like to get his hands on.

00:08:24.350 --> 00:08:29.320
My elder brother has boarded the Mystic Eyes
Collection Train in order to get it back.

00:08:29.610 --> 00:08:32.320
Come on, you can't be telling me
to go back him up there!

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:37.240
No. Apparently, it's absolutely impossible
to board that train without an invitation.

00:08:37.490 --> 00:08:40.620
What I need are clues
about the perpetrator.

00:08:41.040 --> 00:08:43.370
I see. So, playing detective...

00:08:43.710 --> 00:08:48.790
We're talking about investigating a perpetrator
who can steal a catalyst from a Lord's vault.

00:08:49.040 --> 00:08:51.590
I need someone who can deal
with things getting a bit rough.

00:08:51.840 --> 00:08:53.130
I see what you're getting at.

00:08:53.380 --> 00:08:56.800
But why aren't you resolving this
within Modern Magecraft Theories?

00:08:57.140 --> 00:09:00.850
Of course, it's because I suspect
someone on the inside the most.

00:09:01.270 --> 00:09:02.600
Isn't that how it goes?

00:09:03.310 --> 00:09:04.480
Indeed.

00:09:05.350 --> 00:09:07.980
Oh, and I'll give you an assistant.

00:09:08.230 --> 00:09:09.610
A reliable one.

00:09:15.070 --> 00:09:18.070
Lord El-Melloi II's Case Files
｛Rail Zeppelin｝ Grace note

00:09:24.870 --> 00:09:27.580
Oh, little apprentice! Over here!

00:09:29.920 --> 00:09:31.090
Will you take this plate?

00:09:33.960 --> 00:09:35.630
Why don't you order something?

00:09:35.840 --> 00:09:40.390
Oh no. I'm not feeling too well.

00:09:40.720 --> 00:09:41.850
Oh, I see.

00:09:42.100 --> 00:09:43.060
What about Sir?

00:09:43.060 --> 00:09:44.520
Oh, not yet.

00:09:44.770 --> 00:09:47.020
I'm sure it's something like him
asking for five more minutes

00:09:47.020 --> 00:09:49.060
because he's not a good riser, right?

00:09:49.810 --> 00:09:51.070
<i>Five more minutes.</i>

00:09:51.900 --> 00:09:53.690
You really know a lot.

00:09:54.280 --> 00:09:56.950
Of course, I want to be his mistress.

00:09:58.410 --> 00:10:00.700
"A mistress," you say?

00:10:03.330 --> 00:10:05.200
You're not fazed by this comment.

00:10:05.450 --> 00:10:07.870
I guess you're not a rival, then.

00:10:08.500 --> 00:10:09.960
The Mystic Eyes of Viewing Emotions.

00:10:10.290 --> 00:10:14.300
My family's Magecraft cuts gems
and turns them into Mystic Eyes.

00:10:14.840 --> 00:10:17.130
This one can see human emotions.

00:10:17.550 --> 00:10:18.720
I'm sorry.

00:10:18.970 --> 00:10:21.390
What comment should I have been fazed by?

00:10:24.560 --> 00:10:25.680
I see.

00:10:25.930 --> 00:10:27.890
This isn't worth my time.

00:10:29.770 --> 00:10:30.980
Welcome, sir!

00:10:31.860 --> 00:10:32.820
Yvette...

00:10:33.150 --> 00:10:34.360
Now, now, come on over!

00:10:34.820 --> 00:10:36.900
Your cute apprentice is here, too!

00:10:42.200 --> 00:10:43.660
How was it?

00:10:44.160 --> 00:10:48.290
I asked the conductor
about who sent us the invitation.

00:10:48.660 --> 00:10:53.040
He said it was one of the free slot invitations
that are handed out to several people.

00:10:53.290 --> 00:10:57.460
They don't know who originally had
this invitation, either.

00:10:57.720 --> 00:10:59.050
I see.

00:11:00.590 --> 00:11:03.470
Quite a few free slot invites are sent out.

00:11:03.470 --> 00:11:04.560
Is that so?

00:11:04.850 --> 00:11:08.680
If they don't invite new people,
the auction becomes too routine.

00:11:09.020 --> 00:11:11.980
There should be over a dozen
of those sent out every year.

00:11:13.690 --> 00:11:16.570
So, we won't be able to trace them
through the invitation.

00:11:16.820 --> 00:11:18.030
That's impossible.

00:11:18.280 --> 00:11:21.360
More like you could've asked me
instead of Caules

00:11:21.360 --> 00:11:23.620
if it was something about this train!

00:11:23.870 --> 00:11:26.830
Why I didn't do so
will be the topic for your self-study!

00:11:27.950 --> 00:11:31.500
That's so cruel! You're so mean, sir!

00:11:33.080 --> 00:11:36.750
Now, please bait them out well,

00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:38.550
Great Detective.

00:11:42.340 --> 00:11:43.090
Sir!

00:11:43.640 --> 00:11:45.470
This was wedged into the door.

00:11:45.720 --> 00:11:46.510
Oh.

00:11:48.850 --> 00:11:49.770
This is...

00:11:50.230 --> 00:11:53.600
"I am honored that you noticed the invitation

00:11:53.850 --> 00:11:55.270
and made your way out here."

00:11:56.020 --> 00:11:56.940
Sir...

00:11:57.190 --> 00:11:59.900
Yeah, it's from that thief.

00:12:00.150 --> 00:12:02.910
They want me to head
to the cargo bay at twilight.

00:12:03.160 --> 00:12:04.700
Lord El-Melloi II?

00:12:05.700 --> 00:12:09.040
Do you mind if I speak
with you for a short while?

00:12:09.290 --> 00:12:13.580
I don't know if I can speak of anything
that would win your favor.

00:12:13.960 --> 00:12:16.790
I can't quite say
that I'm a customer for this auction.

00:12:17.040 --> 00:12:21.470
I feel you're the most suited person
in the Clock Tower to talk about this with.

00:12:22.010 --> 00:12:24.970
I mean, it's about the Holy Grail War.

00:12:28.350 --> 00:12:29.720
I'm listening.

00:12:35.520 --> 00:12:38.110
What does Astromancy want to do
with the Holy Grail War?

00:12:38.360 --> 00:12:40.940
How the previous El-Melloi passed away

00:12:41.190 --> 00:12:43.780
was discussed over
at Animusphere, as well.

00:12:43.780 --> 00:12:47.490
Besides, it's so talked about
that you hear of it even if you're a shut-in.

00:12:49.290 --> 00:12:54.420
How you want to join the Holy Grail War
even by mobilizing the Sophia-Ri Family.

00:12:54.710 --> 00:12:59.340
I didn't think Animusphere would be
that interested in the ordinary world.

00:12:59.590 --> 00:13:01.510
This is a fragment of a planet, too.

00:13:01.760 --> 00:13:04.970
Looking at the heavens
and looking at Earth are the same thing.

00:13:05.220 --> 00:13:07.090
Observing the planet.

00:13:07.430 --> 00:13:10.810
We concluded that you came here
to purchase Mystic Eyes

00:13:10.810 --> 00:13:14.350
as a weapon to use in the Holy Grail War.
Are we mistaken?

00:13:15.140 --> 00:13:18.360
That's not exactly correct,
I guess you could say.

00:13:18.610 --> 00:13:23.690
What I want is the eye-catcher
of this auction, Rainbow Mystic Eyes.

00:13:23.690 --> 00:13:25.280
Rainbow Mystic Eyes?

00:13:25.950 --> 00:13:28.620
The ultimate operation of celestial bodies
within the human body!

00:13:28.990 --> 00:13:32.540
I'm not well-versed,
but is it something that amazing?

00:13:32.910 --> 00:13:34.580
Each Mystic Eyes has a rank.

00:13:34.960 --> 00:13:38.460
Higher caliber Mystic Eyes are ranked
as "Gold-class," then "Jewel-class,"

00:13:38.710 --> 00:13:40.590
and "Rainbow-class"
is a rank above those.

00:13:40.880 --> 00:13:42.550
I didn't think it actually existed.

00:13:42.800 --> 00:13:47.220
I believe almost no one at the Clock Tower
has seen Rainbow Mystic Eyes.

00:13:51.430 --> 00:13:53.850
But if such Mystic Eyes
are going to be put up for auction,

00:13:54.100 --> 00:13:58.230
wouldn't you think that I'd purchase it
for the Holy Grail War?

00:13:58.230 --> 00:14:02.190
I don't think El-Melloi in its current state
has that much financial prowess.

00:14:02.610 --> 00:14:04.610
You sure are blunt about it.

00:14:04.860 --> 00:14:10.240
I see. So, you're certain there'll be
Rainbow Mystic Eyes at the auction.

00:14:10.530 --> 00:14:11.910
It's fine, Trisha.

00:14:12.160 --> 00:14:16.120
The talk will go smoother
if we show at least that card to them.

00:14:16.660 --> 00:14:17.750
Understood.

00:14:19.210 --> 00:14:20.170
It's because...

00:14:21.040 --> 00:14:22.670
I had a vision.

00:14:24.840 --> 00:14:26.380
Oh, this is perfect.

00:14:26.630 --> 00:14:28.010
Lord El-Melloi II,

00:14:28.380 --> 00:14:30.300
can you raise your right hand?

00:14:30.550 --> 00:14:31.430
Like this?

00:14:31.850 --> 00:14:32.850
Yes.

00:14:33.310 --> 00:14:35.100
Three, two...

00:14:35.310 --> 00:14:36.100
one.

00:14:37.270 --> 00:14:39.230
I'm sorry! I need to head outside!

00:14:47.990 --> 00:14:50.320
The Mystic Eyes of Premonition, huh?

00:14:50.910 --> 00:14:54.410
I had a vision where Rainbow Mystic Eyes
were put up for auction.

00:14:54.410 --> 00:14:56.830
I'm sorry! Please excuse me!

00:15:01.080 --> 00:15:03.340
So, what do you want me to do?

00:15:03.590 --> 00:15:05.590
When the Rainbow Mystic Eyes come out,

00:15:05.920 --> 00:15:10.590
I want you to bid
if some other fool were to bid for them.

00:15:10.930 --> 00:15:14.850
Oh? You were the one who told me
I don't have the fortune to do that.

00:15:15.140 --> 00:15:20.100
No Mage would be foolish enough
to antagonize two families of Lords, right?

00:15:20.390 --> 00:15:23.730
If you can fold as soon as the others do,

00:15:23.980 --> 00:15:25.820
I can curb the damage to a minimum.

00:15:27.820 --> 00:15:30.070
For now, I'll comply with your request.

00:15:30.650 --> 00:15:31.410
Thank you.

00:15:31.660 --> 00:15:34.120
It helps me out that you can have
constructive conversations.

00:15:34.370 --> 00:15:37.580
I'll give you a suitable reward
if you assist me.

00:15:53.760 --> 00:15:55.800
Are you all right, miss?

00:16:00.060 --> 00:16:01.100
I'm sorry.

00:16:01.520 --> 00:16:03.230
It seems I'm slightly motion sick.

00:16:03.940 --> 00:16:07.980
After all, this train doesn't run
along typical railroad tracks.

00:16:09.280 --> 00:16:15.620
The Mystic Eyes Collection Train
runs along magical tracks built atop Leylines.

00:16:15.870 --> 00:16:17.740
If you're not used to it,
your condition will worsen.

00:16:18.080 --> 00:16:20.450
Get some sugar and hydrate yourself.

00:16:20.700 --> 00:16:22.500
That should make things slightly better.

00:16:22.960 --> 00:16:24.750
Thank you very much.

00:16:36.010 --> 00:16:37.890
A-Are you okay?

00:16:39.430 --> 00:16:41.730
I had no intent of looking.

00:16:42.060 --> 00:16:45.650
I see. So, you're not a Mage.

00:16:45.900 --> 00:16:47.900
The guise of King Arthur...

00:16:48.150 --> 00:16:49.230
Such a thing...

00:16:50.150 --> 00:16:51.360
How do you know that?

00:16:51.570 --> 00:16:52.610
I'm sorry.

00:16:52.900 --> 00:16:55.990
I can see the past with my Mystic Eyes.

00:16:56.240 --> 00:16:58.240
There's no need to see
such things, either.

00:16:58.740 --> 00:17:01.290
Thank you. I'm fine now.

00:17:03.660 --> 00:17:07.290
As you said, I'm not a Mage.

00:17:07.540 --> 00:17:11.050
I call myself "Sir's Apprentice,"
but that's only in name.

00:17:11.670 --> 00:17:16.550
That's why you're unsure of whether or not
you're of any use to the Lord.

00:17:17.050 --> 00:17:18.050
Yes.

00:17:20.180 --> 00:17:24.310
You're fine. You're already
someone he finds necessary.

00:17:24.560 --> 00:17:26.440
I'll guarantee it.

00:17:27.810 --> 00:17:29.570
Is that Magecraft, as well?

00:17:31.480 --> 00:17:32.400
No.

00:17:32.650 --> 00:17:35.450
It's what you call "life experience."

00:17:47.670 --> 00:17:49.630
May I sit next to you?

00:17:50.540 --> 00:17:51.710
You have something else?

00:17:53.460 --> 00:17:56.550
When we did our research
about the previous Holy Grail War,

00:17:56.800 --> 00:18:00.760
we got to know about a boy
named Waver Velvet.

00:18:01.010 --> 00:18:02.310
My oh my.

00:18:02.560 --> 00:18:04.680
Wasn't that a terrible record to see?

00:18:05.520 --> 00:18:07.980
He was only a third-generation Mage.

00:18:08.230 --> 00:18:10.560
He was far from
what you could call promising,

00:18:10.900 --> 00:18:13.190
but he returned alive
from the Holy Grail War.

00:18:16.110 --> 00:18:19.070
However, upon return,
he was resolved to do something

00:18:19.320 --> 00:18:22.280
and succeeded the El-Melloi family,
now being called a "Lord."

00:18:22.620 --> 00:18:24.500
Only in name.

00:18:25.540 --> 00:18:31.340
That must mean the Holy Grail War
was a large turning point in his life.

00:18:31.590 --> 00:18:32.550
For instance,

00:18:34.210 --> 00:18:36.550
meeting a hero of yore.

00:18:38.260 --> 00:18:40.050
An interesting speculation.

00:18:40.510 --> 00:18:41.350
Yes,

00:18:41.600 --> 00:18:43.930
one more to add
to speculation.

00:18:44.350 --> 00:18:48.310
If you were to summon
the same Heroic Spirit once again,

00:18:48.940 --> 00:18:50.730
wouldn't the Servant
have no memories

00:18:50.730 --> 00:18:53.770
of racing through this world with you?

00:18:58.070 --> 00:19:01.570
I'm surprised that Astromancy
was interested in things as such.

00:19:01.820 --> 00:19:04.240
That definitely is something
that has nothing to do with the stars.

00:19:04.490 --> 00:19:08.080
They say that connections
are similar to stars, you know.

00:19:08.750 --> 00:19:11.210
There's something
I'd like to ask myself.

00:19:11.460 --> 00:19:15.960
What kind of Rainbow Mystic Eyes
did you folks have a vision of?

00:19:16.510 --> 00:19:19.590
I believe we have no need
to tell you that much in detail.

00:19:19.880 --> 00:19:22.340
No matter which Mystic Eyes
Collection Train you're on,

00:19:22.600 --> 00:19:26.350
I cannot imagine them being able to ready
two sets of Rainbow-class Mystic Eyes at once.

00:19:27.180 --> 00:19:29.600
I see, that is reasonable.

00:19:30.060 --> 00:19:32.270
Humans live being dependent
on information,

00:19:32.270 --> 00:19:34.480
and they die being bound
by information.

00:19:35.020 --> 00:19:38.400
Of which, vision provides
the largest amount of information.

00:19:38.650 --> 00:19:41.740
Vision is the first Magecraft
in human history.

00:19:41.990 --> 00:19:46.240
To incorporate information can be said
as the foundation of Magecraft.

00:19:50.750 --> 00:19:55.040
That is why humans are dominated
by memories, by information.

00:19:55.590 --> 00:20:00.840
To have Mystic Eyes is to accept
the destiny of being bound by them.

00:20:01.090 --> 00:20:02.760
If you are going to purchase Mystic Eyes,

00:20:03.010 --> 00:20:05.180
please take that
into careful consideration.

00:20:05.430 --> 00:20:07.560
I'm greatly obliged by your advice.

00:20:11.440 --> 00:20:15.270
<i>This train will stop
at this location for about two hours.</i>

00:20:15.270 --> 00:20:23.570
<i>You are free to spend this time either
aboard the train or wandering outside...</i>

00:20:32.290 --> 00:20:33.580
Sir...

00:20:34.250 --> 00:20:38.420
Have you heard something
about myself and the Holy Grail War?

00:20:38.630 --> 00:20:39.760
No.

00:20:40.170 --> 00:20:42.840
No, but such a...

00:20:44.090 --> 00:20:48.430
Servants don't have memories
of previous summons, huh?

00:20:48.680 --> 00:20:52.180
That was something
I've understood for the longest time.

00:20:52.180 --> 00:20:55.190
But sir, if there is someone
you are devoted to,

00:20:55.190 --> 00:20:59.360
wanting that person to have memories
of you is only natural, isn't it?

00:21:00.820 --> 00:21:05.200
Right. It's not like I don't care
whether or not he has forgotten me.

00:21:07.830 --> 00:21:10.740
However, there's someone
I want to meet despite all that.

00:21:11.040 --> 00:21:12.620
There is something I want to confirm.

00:21:13.080 --> 00:21:15.500
There is something to settle and finish

00:21:16.130 --> 00:21:18.290
so I can walk past the last ten years.

00:21:22.920 --> 00:21:25.890
Yes, I'm fixated on just that,
something so petty.

00:21:26.390 --> 00:21:28.470
Each of us being remembered

00:21:28.720 --> 00:21:31.270
and being able to relish each other's memories.

00:21:31.520 --> 00:21:35.310
Such happiness is too big a reward
even if it was deferred.

00:21:35.810 --> 00:21:38.900
I can't possibly pay that off in my life.

00:21:39.650 --> 00:21:40.900
Sir...

00:21:45.990 --> 00:21:47.070
Gray!

00:21:47.280 --> 00:21:48.120
Yes!

00:21:53.000 --> 00:21:54.080
This is...

00:21:55.250 --> 00:21:57.580
I was just getting a breath of forest air.

00:21:58.000 --> 00:21:59.000
And...

00:21:59.340 --> 00:22:01.380
when I returned,

00:22:01.380 --> 00:22:02.420
Trisha...

00:22:03.920 --> 00:22:05.050
Trisha was...

00:22:07.050 --> 00:22:10.050
EPISODE 7: Rail Zeppelin 1/6
A Train Whistle of Departure
and the First Murder
